From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:10:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 435/488] [DS4.1] Adaptive verification's draft budget and
 logits rows in TileLang

The draft budget (_assign_draft_token_budget) took about thirteen torch
launches whenever the budget trimmed the drafts: the gather, cumprod,
mask, topk, index_fill and sum. One block now reproduces it bit for bit:
the survival products in cumprod's order (CUB's sequential scan for one
request, tensor_kernel_scan_innermost_dim's Sklansky scan for several),
torch.topk's ranking by radix key (NaN first, ties to the lower slot)
and each request's admitted count.

The offsets kernel also writes the expanded state indices and positions
of each request's logits rows, so production's path (adaptive
verification) no longer launches expand_idx_mapping, which run 17 still
timed 0.03 us slower than Triton. Without adaptive verification the
expand kernel serves as before.
